<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "TEST-6: After reviewing the proposed approach, I recommend we keep the golden file checked into the repository rather than generating it at CI startup. The checked-in file gives reviewers a diff surface: when a classifier change lands, the PR must also include an updated snapshot-golden.json, making"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/kg/onto#Decision> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAttributedTo> <https://example.org/kg/resource/person/carol> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://example.org/kg/resource/issue/TEST-6> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasGeneratedBy> <https://example.org/kg/resource/run/golden-run> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <https://example.org/kg/onto#detail> "After reviewing the proposed approach, I recommend we keep the golden file checked into the repository rather than generating it at CI startup. The checked-in file gives reviewers a diff surface: when a classifier change lands, the PR must also include an updated snapshot-golden.json, making the impact immediately visible. The alternative of generating at test time and comparing to a reference stored in environment variables hides the delta from PR reviewers. The checked-in approach also supports the offline workflow: a developer can run the test locally without network access and still get the correct verdict. One concern is that the golden must be regenerated deliberately via the --write flag rather than automatically on every test run. We address this by making the --write path the only sanctioned update mechanism and documenting it in the error message printed on failure." .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-6/0> <https://example.org/kg/onto#tagged> <https://example.org/kg/resource/topic/architecture> .
