<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/0> <https://example.org/kg/onto#detail> "# ai-implement-kg-refresh-learnings\n\nThe kg-refresh run revealed that the snapshot guard rule fires correctly when comment.nt shrinks. The zero-shrink rule prevented a silent data loss when the tracker API returned an empty page due to a transient network error. The fix is to always check issue_count before applying the zero-shrink threshold." .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/0> <https://example.org/kg/onto#fix> "# ai-implement-kg-refresh-learnings\n\nThe kg-refresh run revealed that the snapshot guard rule fires correctly when comment.nt shrinks. The zero-shrink rule prevented a silent data loss when the tracker API returned an empty page due to a transient network error. The fix is to always check issue_count before applying the zero-shrink threshold." .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/0> <https://example.org/kg/onto#tagged> <https://example.org/kg/resource/topic/snapshot> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "TEST-8: After reviewing the guard integration, the team agreed that the zero-shrink rule should apply only when the tracker returns at least one issue, not when the issue count is zero. This decision preserves backward compatibility for repos that do not configure a tracker team in sources.yml, wher"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://example.org/kg/onto#Decision> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAttributedTo> <https://example.org/kg/resource/person/dave> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://example.org/kg/resource/issue/TEST-8> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasGeneratedBy> <https://example.org/kg/resource/run/golden-run> .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <https://example.org/kg/onto#detail> "<!-- orchestrator context: TEST-8 review -->\n\nAfter reviewing the guard integration, the team agreed that the zero-shrink rule should apply only when the tracker returns at least one issue, not when the issue count is zero. This decision preserves backward compatibility for repos that do not configure a tracker team in sources.yml, where every run would otherwise fail the zero-shrink check. The threshold-only rule still applies to code-derived parts such as commit.nt and file.nt, which can legitimately shrink when commits are pruned or files are deleted. This distinction between tracker-derived and code-derived parts is the key architectural decision here." .
<https://example.org/kg/resource/comment/TEST-8/1> <https://example.org/kg/onto#tagged> <https://example.org/kg/resource/topic/snapshot> .
